The other two blockers: the growth-arrow claim asserts she's integrating toward Four (turning attention inward) twenty lines before the closing says locating her own needs has never occurred to her — plus it carries a factual error the packet already caught (CLM-22: the gown predates the exhibition). And the childhood section's "The surplus has a start date" is a childhood-wound etiology claim, which the house Type 2 pillar explicitly refuses (*"it can't tell anyone how you were raised"*) and the project's standing do-not-write list prohibits; it also swaps her stated motive — *"I didn't want the show to end"* — for a man about to "stop paying attention to her."

